        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 90-year-old male patient from 14th to 15th December 2018. He was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infectious or other systemic causes. He was promptly treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, leading to satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were closely monitored throughout his stay. The patient was discharged in a stable condition and I kindly ask you to continue monitoring his respiratory status and adjust maintenance therapy accordingly. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
